#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
PI AF / OSIsoft PI Analysis Excel export -> RapidMiner-ready workbook.

Usage from command prompt:
  python pi_af_full_pipeline_jupyter_updated.py --input sample_analysis.xlsx --output pi_af_analysis_rapidminer_final.xlsx
  python pi_af_full_pipeline_jupyter_updated.py --input sample_analysis.xlsx --output pi_af_analysis_rapidminer_final.xlsx --sheet Sheet1
  python pi_af_full_pipeline_jupyter_updated.py --input sample_analysis.xlsx --output final.xlsx --tagval-base-minutes 15

Usage from Jupyter Notebook:
  1. Put this whole script in one cell, or open it as a notebook/script.
  2. Update JUPYTER_INPUT_FILE, JUPYTER_OUTPUT_FILE, and JUPYTER_SHEET_NAME below.
  3. Run the cell.

Input workbook expected columns:
  Column A / header Name                         = Analysis name
  Column B / header AnalysisRuleConfigString     = PI AF calculation string
  Column C / header AnalysisRuleVariableMapping  = PI AF output variable mapping

The script uses openpyxl only, preserves duplicate formula rows, and creates
RapidMiner-ready formula/input sheets.
"""

